[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says the date reports are one issue with one fix queued. The desk's own
table below says otherwise: the reports merged into it have more than one cause. They were merged on
subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and "wrong date" is a
subject that more than one bug produces.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 is the parser fix. It does nothing for the <code>hint</code> reports or the
one-day moves: they now have their own tickets.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table is the desk's own view, built from the export when the page renders. It shows three
problems, and each now has a ticket:

- the `parser` row, without the reports in its footnote → [#1 parser reads day-first dates month first](https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows-4/issues/1)
- the `hint` row, "no ticket of its own" until now → [#2 booking form hint tells day-first tenants to type month first](https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows-4/issues/2)
- the footnote, the reports read as a one-day move → [#3 one-day move, read by the desk as not a swap](https://github.com/ciborro/mega-what-it-shows-4/issues/3)

Each ticket states how many reports it covers, counted as the table counts them.

## What each problem is

**`parser`** — the shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get day and month
swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July.

**`hint`** — `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first, as told,
and the form reads the value the tenant's way. Same symptom as `parser`, different code, different
fix.

**one-day move** — the reports in the table's footnote (`desk-notes.json`). They are not a day/month
swap: a date moved by one day, or different days in different time zones. The table files them under
`parser` by tenant, but the parser fix will not touch them.

## For the desk

- Merge into a ticket only reports with the same cause, not the same subject.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser; place a report by its tenant, as the table does.

